# Godot
.godot/
.import/
export.cfg
export_presets.cfg
*.translation

# Editor-generated resource id sidecars. Only the six from the first unit that
# ran the editor were ever tracked, so every later worker was told to build the
# editor cache and then found a dirty worktree full of files that looked
# committable. Probed before removing them: nothing here resolves a resource by
# uid, the two `uid://` strings in the repo are `[gd_scene]` self-declarations
# rather than `ext_resource` references, and with every .uid deleted the suite
# is green at 217 assertions with no `invalid UID` warning. Godot regenerates
# them on the next editor pass.
*.uid

# Go
/server/bin/
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Local
.env
*.local

# Agent worktrees
.claude/worktrees/
